    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cb773ece",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: can-you-tag-your-friend; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows a baby orangutan with text that reads 'can you tag your friend tell them i found their baby pic.' This meme uses the visual of an infant primate to create a humorous, absurd scenario where the viewer is encouraged to share a picture of a baby animal as if it were a human baby. While not overtly abusive or hateful toward any specific group, the meme relies on the visual similarity between human infants and baby primates to generate humor. The intent is to provoke laughter through the unexpected juxtaposition of the text and the image, playing on the idea of 'baby' as a term that can be applied to both humans and animals. The meme is not inherently toxic, but it does contain a subtle element of anthropomorphism that could be seen as infantilizing or dehumanizing in a broader context, though not in a targeted or harmful way toward any specific group. The overall intent is to entertain through absurdity and the unexpected association of a baby animal with human social media behavior.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_bd97a524"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
